cy rate is cut below 2.5% nominal — the disinflationary-stagnation branch arriving early, most plausibly via the AI-Q4 capex impairment leaving excess datacenter and generation capacity as a deflationary power-price impulse.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my front-loaded inflation object, which is the basis of both CQ2 and the CQ6 inflation cuts. CQ2 falls from 27 to roughly 14-16; CQ6-D rises from 15 to ~24 and CQ6-C falls from 22 to ~13; CQ4 P50 falls 30-40bp as both r* and the term premium ease into a demand shortfall; hypothesis plank (c) rises from 42 toward 60, since 'falls in the 2030s' would be vindicated.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 2 bayes seat, effort 'rstar'."}}